Package: RegCompassR
Title: Multiome Regulatory Evidence and Metabolic Reaction Analysis
Version: 1.9.0
Authors@R: c(person(given = "RegCompass", family = "Developers", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "dev@example.com"))
Author: RegCompass Developers [aut, cre]
Maintainer: RegCompass Developers <dev@example.com>
Description: Fits one cell-type-level sparse-group multi-task Pando model across
    conditions for Human-GEM or Mouse-GEM GPR target genes in paired single-cell
    RNA and ATAC data. The shared TF-peak-target edge dictionary produces a
    universal cell-type GRN, condition-level GRNs, and explicit condition effects.
    Active condition-level edges define metabolic target genes and complete-GPR
    core reactions, while condition effects are projected through metacell
    TF-expression by peak-accessibility interactions to modify reaction penalties.
    Annotation-defined biological meta-modules are deduplicated into a merged
    reaction catalogue without local FASTCORE completion. For each medium
    scenario, the package constructs one shared union GEM and performs a single
    global FASTCORE completion before directional COMPASS-like scoring. A
    post-Layer-2 step can use any GEM reaction as a direct KEGG, Reactome, or
    master-Rhea mapping anchor and score linked non-core reactions in the exact
    cached medium-specific union GEM used for the original analysis. Pinned human
    and mouse GEMs are bundled for offline use, with platform-aware parallel
    execution and audited progress and timing output.
